Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-30-2001||05:26 PM||||Did anyone build their own v8 setup in their fiero?<P>And do you use it as a daily driver?<P><BR>I am on a budget, and have fulltime access to a garage with pit/lift/torches/welders (And know how to use them)<BR>and I have a 350 carbed engine sitting here out of my 75 LT1 Camaro..  <P>Any suggestions/warnings on making my own setup for it?   <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by isthiswhereiputausername? (edited 06-30-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Jason Kamrud||06-30-2001||07:40 PM||||I have been thinking about trying to do my own V8 conversion also, and on as tight of a budget as possible.  I built a really tough 283 that's ready to go in, but before I tear my daily driver '86 SE apart I want to kind of plan out what needs to be done.<P>From what I figure, most of it will be pretty simple except the flywheel. I will either have to build a custom flywheel & starter mounts or buy something aftermarket. The bellhousing adapter should be pretty simple, as with motor mounts. I plan on using the stock clutch b/c you can't get a much bigger clutch into that bellhousing.  Otherwise it should work pretty slick, as long as I get the clearances right on the throwout bearing/clutch fork/slave cylinder so that I can still get the thing to shift smooth.<BR>But right now I've got more time than money, so I think I will give it a try myself & see what happens...I am a hillbilly hot-rodder, and I have done lots of unusual things with pretty good luck, so I will see how much damage I can do to my litte Fiero.  <BR>Archie really knows what he's doing with these Fiero's, and I don't want to take any business away from him, but I really can't afford to buy a whole kit from him right now, so please keep me posted with any cheap & useful advice you recieve!<P>------------------<BR>Jason Kamrud||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||06-30-2001||08:14 PM||||Famous last words. Best of luckto you anyways.||||reg||1
Z||000003||gtcash||06-30-2001||11:58 PM||||Archie sells parts!<BR>Don't try to re-invent the wheel...<BR>Archie has already done it, use his expertise, he's a good guy. He'll talk to you and give you some good advise.<BR>Remember, that cluth and flywheel is only inches from your backsides, spinning at many RPM's...a screwup here means a dis-ass-ter!<BR>Keep it simple and GOOD LUCK, a V8 swap is awesome!||||reg||1
Z||000004||isthiswhereiputausername?||07-01-2001||12:17 AM||||I know I will need to contact Archie on a few parts, (flywheel,etc) but I'm looking on getting the majority of it done myself due to budgets.. ||||reg||1
